  "worked_solution": "The matrix $U$ in the LU decomposition is obtained from the original matrix $A$ by row-reducing using Gaussian elementation. In particular, to make zeros below the main diagonal, we proceed as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =[\\begin{aligned}4 & 7 & -5 \\\\ -4 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 8 & -4 & 7\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+1{R}_{1} \\\\  & \u223c[\\begin{aligned}4 & 7 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 9 & -4 \\\\ 8 & -4 & 7\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-2){R}_{1} \\\\  & \u223c[\\begin{aligned}4 & 7 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 9 & -4 \\\\ 0 & -18 & 17\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we want to make $0$ at the position ${a}_{32}$ using Gaussian elimination. To do this, we take the $3$rd row of $A,$ and we add the $2$nd row of $A$ multiplied by $2:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,[\\begin{aligned}4 & 7 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 9 & -4 \\\\ 0 & -18 & 17\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+2{R}_{2} \\\\  & \u223c[\\begin{aligned}4 & 7 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 9 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 9\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe entry ${l}_{32}$ of the matrix $L$ is the factor next to ${R}_{2},$ taken with the opposite sign:\n\n$$\n{l}_{32}=-(2)=-2.\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
  "fields": [],
